 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "A positive central representative",
 "statement": "Every semisimple represented degree datum ([d-monodromy])\nadmits a positive central pair ([d-central]) $(N,z)$, that is $N>0$ and\n$z\\in Z(G)\\cap HF^N$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-algebraic-groups-lie-algebras/sk-p-central/p-central.md",
  "place": "node p-central, order 2527"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "d-monodromy",
  "d-central"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The finite component group from [lem-wf-algebraic-component-cosets]\nsupplies $m>0$ with $F^m\\in G^\\circ$. By [p-product], factor $F^m=ch$ with\n$c\\in Z(G^\\circ)^\\circ$ and $h\\in H^\\circ$, and choose a finite list\n$g_1,\\ldots,g_r$ meeting every coset of $G^\\circ$ exactly once. Put\n\n$$\nN=mr,\\qquad z=\\prod_{i=1}^r g_i c g_i^{-1}.\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "lem-wf-algebraic-component-cosets",
    "p-product"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Since $G^\\circ$ is normal, all\nconjugates of $c$ lie in its abelian center. Replacing a coset\nrepresentative by $g_i u$, $u\\in G^\\circ$, leaves its factor unchanged;\nthe factors commute. Left multiplication permutes the component cosets,\nso conjugation by any $g\\in G$ fixes their product $z$.\nBy [lem-ag-closure-commutators], every commutator in $G$ lies in $H$,\nso $g_icg_i^{-1}=(g_icg_i^{-1}c^{-1})c\\in Hc$; and\n$c=F^mh^{-1}\\in F^mH=HF^m$ because $H$ is normal.\nThus each $g_i c g_i^{-1}$ has the same $H$-coset as $c$, namely\n$HF^m$, and multiplication yields $z\\in HF^{mr}$.\nThere is at least the identity coset, so $r>0$ and $N=mr>0$.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-ag-closure-commutators"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
